  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Before letting Kostya leave for his supposed shift at the sports bar, Nastya makes him take off his suit jacket and put on an animal-protection shirt, then insists on riding with him to Tretyakovka.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Снимай давай этот пиджак быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Вот, надень эту футболку сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Так удобнее, будто ты на акции.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ладно, спасибо тебе большое, любимая.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "И далеко твой бар находится?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да нет, это совсем рядом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "У меня там магазин сыроедения.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Хочешь, мы вместе туда поедем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, давай поедем туда вместе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Всё, я собираюсь, и мы едем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вот мы уже и пришли.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Давай аккуратненько, я люблю тебя.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Снимай давай этот пиджак быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Take off that suit jacket quickly.' Nastya anchors the line on 'take off', while 'faster' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Вот, надень эту футболку сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Here, put on this T-shirt right now.' The grammar packs 'here' and 'now' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Так удобнее, будто ты на акции.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is more comfortable this way, as if you were at the rally.' In Russian, the idea of 'so' flows naturally into 'rally' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ладно, спасибо тебе большое, любимая.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Alright, thank you very much, sweetheart.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'all right' and finishing on 'favourite'. Nastya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "И далеко твой бар находится?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And is your bar located far from here?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'and' and finishing on 'is located'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да нет, это совсем рядом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not really, it is right nearby.' Notice how Russian expresses 'yes' and 'beside' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "У меня там магазин сыроедения.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My raw-food shop is right over there.' Notice how Russian expresses 'at' and 'raw foodism' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Хочешь, мы вместе туда поедем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you want us to ride there together?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'want' before landing on 'will go'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, давай поедем туда вместе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, let us ride over there together.' Kostya anchors the line on 'yes', while 'together' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Всё, я собираюсь, и мы едем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Alright, I am getting ready, and we are going.' Notice the reflexive suffix on the verb meaning 'intend', turning the action back on the subject. Kostya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вот мы уже и пришли.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Here we have arrived already.' Kostya brings out the contrast between 'here' and 'we' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Давай аккуратненько, я люблю тебя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Take care, I love you.' In Russian, the idea of 'come on' flows naturally into 'you' without extra filler words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
